      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this a config option instead of an optional parameter for the device-mapper target?  See: verity_parse_opt_args().  There are already other optional parameters such as \"ignore_corruption\" and \"restart_on_corruption\".  It\u0027s generally frowned on to put policy in the kernel instead of in userspace.  I think it will be hard to get this change upstream as a config option.\n\nThe \"at least once\" verbiage is also confusing; it really should be \"at most once\", shouldn\u0027t it?  I understand that due to races the verification might actually happen multiple times for a particular block, but \"at most once\" would seem to better describe the intent.  And blocks that are never read are still not verified at all, are they?",
      "revId": "8dc7e00b86bc36bbf552e32d6c83fcf3b6908a43",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
